### Description

`Tensor<T>` currently produces incorrect results if both inputs are slices of the same size from buffers of the same size.

### Reproduction Steps

```csharp
using System.Buffers;
using System.Numerics.Tensors;

TensorSpan<int> x = Tensor.Create<int>([4]);
TensorSpan<int> y = Tensor.Create<int>([4]);

TensorSpan<int> z = x.Slice(0..3);
TensorSpan<int> w = y.Slice(0..3);

x[0] = 0;
x[1] = 1;
x[2] = 2;
x[3] = 3;

x.CopyTo(y);

Console.WriteLine(Tensor.Dot<int>(x, y));
Console.WriteLine(Tensor.Dot<int>(z, w));
```

### Expected behavior

This should print
```
14
5
```

### Actual behavior

This actually prints:
```
14
14
```

